# Nihon-Go! (Cornerstone) — the stack that is running

**Next.js App Router · React 19 · TypeScript · MUI 6 · Better Auth · Payload CMS ·
Postgres on Neon (Drizzle + Payload) · Vercel.**

The repo root **is** the app. `src/` is the Next project; `npm` commands run from the
root.

**Read [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) before writing code.** It is the full orientation —
architecture, the content module, auth, the Payload admin, and which of this repo's
docs are historical. This file only carries the traps that bite before you get there.

## Four traps

- **`client/` and `server/` are dead.** They are the retired CRA + Express + MongoDB
  app, kept only so the cutover stays reversible, deleted at
  [CUTOVER.md](mdc:CUTOVER.md) step 10 (#42). Nothing in them runs, and they contain
  **same-named components that are not interchangeable** with the live ones in `src/`.
  Check which tree a filename belongs to before editing it.

- **Lessons are one collection, two players.** A `lessons` document's `format` field
  decides: `flashcard` → `/lesson/<slug>`, the prefecture player; `step` →
  `/newlesson/<slug>`, the grammar player. When a request says "lesson", establish
  which format it means before picking files — the exercise components are
  format-specific and **not 1:1 interchangeable**.

- **Migration order is fixed.** `npm run db:migrate` before `npm run payload:migrate` —
  Payload never issues `CREATE SCHEMA`, so Drizzle has to create `payload` first. There
  is also no local Postgres: every developer works against a **Neon branch**. See
  [docs/database-workflow.md](mdc:docs/database-workflow.md).

- **Airtable is gone.** It was a mid-migration content backend, replaced by Payload.
  No dependency, no `/api/revalidate` route, no live `AIRTABLE_*` or
  `REVALIDATE_SECRET`. Any doc or comment saying otherwise is history.

## Verifying a change

There is no test suite. `npm run typecheck` plus `npm run parity [url]` are the check,
and both must pass before calling something done. Node 24, pinned in `.nvmrc`.
